<font size=10>Chevtahvtee b'mahryayshahteeot biv
Thanks to all our [fans] (Cyan)

<PB><a name=AP><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>Atrus' Prayer
<font size=10>(1996 Myst Calendar)<font style=n><p align=left>

Ahvo
Kodokhahntor femahgenteeom.
Kodokahnrad kam lorahg kenen b'ken shin
b-baykh b'totee rahnahl tso mahrntahvom.
Doprahchizen b'zoo dho muhkhon b'tayroosh
lemahrnem met misho tsahv te.
Gahth t'dho kenen - dhozonesh tayroo
t'bahshtee vaht - khahgem gahth b'taygahn khezoo.
Pahrkh b'shem.
Kam shin bahrtah t'gestoy rilnahr b'fahsee
domahdho t'pahrahthom gahhootsaythom.

Votahr ah'shem khekamrov kenem.
G'chev ah'shem khekam l'ahrtahem gah kam
boahrtahem.
Ken chevet oyn mor'okh'mor kokenen
remesfet b'vaynuh t'khoytahg zuh tsoshem
g'bortahom.

<PB><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>Atrus' Prayer
<font size=10>(1996 Myst Calendar)<font style=n><p align=left>

[Father?]
I was [reflecting?] [on] your [powers?].
I was thinking what [grace?] it is to be able to link to various places of your creation.
It is [amazing?] to me how complex to [?] you have created this universe I live in.
Still with how it is - [however?] [?] with five [senses?] - you still choose to love for me.
I [pray?] to you.
What I can [accomplish?] by entirely insignificant art I am [achieving?] by your greatness and holiness.
I praise you for who you are.
And I thank you for what you have [allowed?] and what you will [allow?].
I am [thankful] [for my sake?] [grandmother] was diligent to [ask?] with end [result?] about you and your [purpose?].


<a href=#index><p align=right>@<a link=clear>
<PB><a name=GJ><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>Gehn's Journal
<font size=10>(Riven Soundtrack Booklet)<font style=n><p align=left>

Loymaht lekeneet dhaynoytee
pahrah tresheegah reendaytahntee leshuhfayeet
oolbahoy fesev 98 kodobeerah reteejuh
kahg. Ril leeahm lekenen hoosahtay
b'fahsee okh een okh mishtahtahvoy met
fahm gatah chilesh brevog wotsah okh
r'ahchah te ah sev mot.

Khoy regedee kat kolkenen remooshee
greoonahn cheto okh rezeeway ril
bodolpaypeel. Kokenen revog
miro okh revaiduh mot kopoogoen
b'ken erth nuhdahtahv b'rish be erth
teejah teegahl kerah.

Volah tesot prin fahets teegtahntee
kodoteegeet rilte reahreeuhtahv tsahroo
tseemahahl koneetsahvayeet tanuhth
iglahrno temo kokeelaheet kat erth
gahrtahvotee khah treahchah. Bree pahm
sen kotanuheet tsahnosh trefahdho.

Reyeepay kolaneet me gormot
tetemo kojahgahen ahreeuhtahv fooruh
loymaht reloopahtee mot komahrenteet
khahpo kokeneet pekay b'rish be motee.

<PB><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>Gehn's Journal
<font size=10>(Riven Soundtrack Booklet)<font style=n><p align=left>

Though there have been great setbacks in the [way] the Builders have finished my office on Age 233 I was keeping the original [squad]. No question [it] has been [difficult?] to the greatest extent of [any] of my construction this far due mainly to the harsh nature of the [air?] [within] that age.

If the only [surprise (?)] had been the [???] and the hostile disposition of the weather I would not have been [upset?]. It was the toxic nature of the atmosphere that [proved?] to be a major [hindrance?] to a brave working [squad].


Yes, our first small group of workers working without the necessary [eye?] protection suffered temporary [blind]ness [after?] they [spent?] just a few gahrtavotee in the [air?]. Two or three were [blinded?] permanently by the experience.

The eyeglasses they [wore?] from that time [onwards?] [provided?] sufficient protection though the [risks?] which followed perhaps were very insidious (compared) to those.
<a href=#index><p align=right>@<a link=clear>
